+      "logical_name": "three-obstacle-loewner-probe-jet-matrix",
+      "kind": "definition",
+      "title": "Three-obstacle Loewner probe jet matrix",
+      "statement": "For a capacity-2 chordal Loewner chain with real driver W and three obstacle-removal conformal maps h_i analytic near W with h_i'(W)>0, set u_i=h_i''(W)/h_i'(W) and c_i=h_i'''(W)/h_i'(W). The three-probe jet matrix J has row i equal to (u_i,c_i,u_i^2). This is algebraic independence of coefficient tests, not probabilistic independence of the obstacles.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
+        "Three conformal maps analytic near the same driver",
+        "Positive map derivatives"
+      ],
+      "domain": "probability theory; Loewner evolution",
+      "source": {
+        "source_id": "owner-own-work:w399:p0003-three-probe-20261010",
+        "url": "file:///~/brain_workers/w399/LEMMA_THREE_PROBE.md",
+        "revision": "author-derived-2026-10-10-pending-w401",
+        "license": "owner-own-work (campaign auxiliary proof; independent review pending)",
+        "excerpt": null
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "key": "identification",
+      "namespace": "probability.sle",
+      "logical_name": "localized-three-probe-loewner-characteristic-identification",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "DRAFT: local three-probe Loewner characteristic identification",
+      "statement": "Author-derived conditional result, pending independent review: let a capacity-2 chordal Loewner driver be a continuous semimartingale dW=mu dt+dN, with N a continuous local martingale and d<N>=v dt, v>=0 and locally integrable coefficients. Fix constant alpha>0. Before three fixed obstacles are hit, let h_i be their hydrodynamic maps, analytic at W with positive derivative. If each h_i'(W)^alpha is a local martingale on a common positive interval and the matrix with rows (h_i''/h_i',h_i'''/h_i',(h_i''/h_i')^2) is invertible for a.e. time there, then mu=0 and v=8/3 a.e. there and alpha=5/8. Global Brownian-driver/SLE identification additionally needs such intervals to cover all finite times.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
+        "Continuous semimartingale driver with absolutely continuous drift/quadratic variation",
+        "Capacity normalization partial_t g=2/(g-W)",
+        "Common constant alpha>0",
+        "Reflected analytic conformal derivatives and local boundedness stops",
+        "Three local martingales over an interval",
+        "A.e. nondegenerate jet matrix",
+        "Globalization requires explicit coverage of all finite times"
+      ],
+      "domain": "probability theory; Loewner evolution",
+      "source": {
+        "source_id": "owner-own-work:w399:p0003-three-probe-20261010",
+        "url": "file:///~/brain_workers/w399/LEMMA_THREE_PROBE.md",
+        "revision": "author-derived-2026-10-10-pending-w401",
+        "license": "owner-own-work (campaign auxiliary proof; independent review pending)",
+        "excerpt": null
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "key": "stability",
+      "namespace": "probability.sle",
+      "logical_name": "three-vertical-slit-probe-characteristic-stability",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "DRAFT: quantitative three-slit characteristic stability",
+      "statement": "At the three-slit initial jet matrix J=[[-1/2,-3/4,1/4],[1/2,-3/4,1/4],[-3/4,-9/16,9/16]], corresponding to slit locations/heights (1,1),(-1,1),(1,sqrt(3)), define normalized drift residuals e=J(mu,v/2-4/3,[1+v(alpha-1)]/2). If |e_i|<=epsilon, then |mu|<=2epsilon, |v-8/3|<=(52/9)epsilon and |1+v(alpha-1)|<=(40/3)epsilon. If v>=v_min>0, also |alpha-5/8|<=(31/(2v_min))epsilon. The inverse matrix norm in maximum absolute row sum is 20/3. These are fixed-configuration bounds, pending independent review, with no SAW residual estimate asserted.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
+        "Exactly the displayed jet configuration",
+        "Residual normalized by alpha times the derivative-power process",
+        "Positive variance lower bound required for the exponent estimate",
+        "No global uniform jet control is assumed"
+      ],
+      "domain": "probability theory; Loewner evolution",
+      "source": {
+        "source_id": "owner-own-work:w399:p0003-three-probe-20261010",
+        "url": "file:///~/brain_workers/w399/LEMMA_THREE_PROBE.md",
+        "revision": "author-derived-2026-10-10-pending-w401",
+        "license": "owner-own-work (campaign auxiliary proof; independent review pending)",
+        "excerpt": null
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "key": "degeneracy",
+      "namespace": "probability.sle",
+      "logical_name": "two-symmetric-slit-initial-tests-do-not-identify-loewner-coefficients",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "DRAFT: two symmetric initial probes leave a coefficient ambiguity",
+      "statement": "For the two symmetric vertical-slit jet rows (-1/2,-3/4,1/4) and (1/2,-3/4,1/4), the coefficient values mu=0,v=14/3,alpha=29/14 give theta=(mu,v/2-4/3,[1+v(alpha-1)]/2)=(0,1,3) and zero initial drift residual in both rows. The third row (-3/4,-9/16,9/16) gives residual 9/8. This exact pointwise algebra does not assert that those wrong coefficients make the first two processes martingales throughout an interval. Independent review is pending.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
+        "Pointwise initial probes only",
