+      "logical_name": "honeycomb-saw-three-probe-route-continuum-and-ensemble-gates",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "P0003 three-probe route: unproved continuum and ensemble inputs",
+      "statement": "The P0003 ledger source, Grimmett arXiv:2205.07318 Question 2.2, concerns uniform n-step honeycomb SAW from the origin under suitable rescaling. A related all-length critical boundary-to-boundary chordal conjecture is Duminil-Copin–Smirnov arXiv:1007.0575 Section 4 Conjecture 1. The w399 three-probe route proves only auxiliary conditional Loewner coefficient identification. Its hardest unproved input is convergence of localized random-domain SAW tail partition martingales to three derivative powers with one common positive exponent. Driver/filtration regularity, global probe coverage, curve convergence and transfer to the fixed-n ensemble are also unproved. Current openness is UNKNOWN; no full scaling-limit proof or novelty is claimed.",
